# --- Working material, deliberately NOT part of the submission ------------
# The story specs are ~3,500 lines of teaching material written while building.
# They are learning notes, not a deliverable, and the proportion against ~900
# lines of source would draw attention to scope rather than rigour.
docs/stories/

# Decision records. The reasoning they hold is summarised in APPROACH.md, which is
# the deliverable the brief actually names; shipping both duplicates the argument.
docs/adr/

# Analysis of the brief itself (what is being graded, traps). Prep material.
docs/OVERVIEW.md

# Index of the above; its links would all dangle.
docs/README.md

# Interview preparation - predicted questions, rehearsed answers, tour route.
# Must never ship.
docs/INTERVIEW-PLAN.md

# File-by-file walkthrough written for rehearsal. Prep material.
docs/CODE-TOUR.md

# Working instructions and conventions, with interview-specific content.
CLAUDE.md

# Claude Code local state.
.claude/

# --- What DOES ship from docs/ -------------------------------------------
#   docs/PROTOCOL.md   wire format, linked from README and APPROACH
#   docs/DEMO.md       the walkthrough, linked from README
#   (nothing else)
